+### Parametric Surface Density Model
+Models density using parametric functions rather than explicit SDFs. Differs by supporting volumetric effects natively instead of relying on surface marching. Choose for fog or smoke. [Parametric Surface Density Model](14736-parametric-surface-density-model.md)
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$ where $N$ is the number of pixels and $S$ is the number of steps (128). The SDF evaluation is $O(1)$ per step [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory. No scene graph or geometry buffers are stored [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$ where $N$ is the number of pixels and $S$ is the number of steps (128). The SDF evaluation is $O(1)$ per step [G].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory. No scene graph or geometry buffers are stored [G].
 *   **Performance:** Runs in real-time on WebGL2-capable hardware. Performance is limited by fragment shader complexity and fill rate [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Infinite procedural generation, no asset loading, deterministic CPU/GPU sync [S1, unofficial].
